# Local maven-publish output (Track 2 / D4). The publishing block writes each module's
# AAR + POM tree into <module>/distribution; it is build output, was committed by accident
# (8.6 MB of stale 6.0.0-beta.1 artifacts) and is regenerated on every publish. Consumers
# fetch from Cloudsmith, so it must never be committed or mirrored.
distribution/

# Secrets and credentials (Track 2 / S3). Never commit new ones. The copies that must exist
# (master apps, push samples) are already tracked on purpose and stay tracked; the release
# mirror deletes the keystores and replaces google-services.json with a placeholder before
# anything reaches the public repo. Adding another needs `git add -f`, which is the point.
google-services.json
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
*.pfx
*.pem
*service-account*.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# External native build folder generated in Android Studio 2.2 and later
.externalNativeBuild


# Freeline
freeline.py
freeline/
freeline_project_description.json

# fastlane
fastlane/report.xml
fastlane/Preview.html
fastlane/screenshots
fastlane/test_output
fastlane/readme.md

# Kiro MCP settings (contains API keys)
.kiro/settings/mcp.json

# Legacy UI Kit module
chatuikit/

# Local screenshot gallery output
#screenshot-gallery/

# Roborazzi snapshot outputs
chatuikit-kotlin/src/test/snapshots/
chatuikit-compose/src/test/snapshots/

# Local E2E credentials for the pre-push gate (scripts/ci-local.sh gate 7).
# Ignored on purpose. ENG-38650 made it a standing decision that a working App ID and Auth
# Key are never committed -- that is why master-app-*/AppCredentials.kt is empty and the
# values are typed into the in-app credentials screen instead. Copy the template and fill
# it in per clone:  cp scripts/e2e-credentials.env.example scripts/e2e-credentials.env
scripts/e2e-credentials.env
